// **Came up on the stairs of somewhere else.**
//
// Arrives already practised at hauling (`SYSTEMS.md` §6.17) and carries
// one more per trip. The one trait that is straightforwardly good, and
// it is bounded by the same argument practice is: a rank is ten
// percent, the ceiling is three, and it cannot be spent or stacked.
//
// What it actually buys is *time* — a tower that recruits one of these
// gets the veteran it would otherwise have spent a day and a half
// making, which matters most in a run that is only half an hour long
// (§6.19).
#![enable(implicit_some)]
TraitDef(
    id: "trait.porter",
    name: "Porter",
    blurb: "knows stairs, and how much a person can carry",
    carry_bonus: 1,
    practised_at: Haul,
)
